enchilada: GPU: one SMMU TLB invalidate per mapped BO, not per 4 KiB page

Boots 24 and 27 (OpenGL ES CoreAnimation at 675 MHz): every GL frame spent ~95 ms in eagl.c's
"before it for the IOSurfaces" (frames came ~100 ms apart, ~9 fps) against ~20 ms in boot 22,
where the SURFACE_BO import of the display surface was refused and only the CPU refill ran. CA's
GL renderer makes a new 1125x2436 display surface every frame (ids 19, 20, 21 ... 56), so every
frame imports 13.9 MB, and mapGem() entered it with sweet_gpu_vm_map(), which ends each 4 KiB
PTE with gpu_tlb_invalidate(): TLBIALL on both context banks and TLBIALLNSNH, each polled over
MMIO -- 3392 times per surface (and 3072 for every fresh 12 MB texture BO). Now the pages go in
with sweet_gpu_vm_map_nosync() and one sweet_gpu_vm_sync() (barrier + the same invalidate) runs
after the last one, before the handle is handed out; GEM_INFO SET_IOVA's remap does the same.
Nothing can use the new range earlier: the GPU only sees an iova once a later SUBMIT names it,
and SUBMIT takes gAdrenoLock, which mapGem holds. Unmapping already invalidated once per range.
The first 8 surface imports log their time ("SWEET GPU: surface N: K KB entered for the GPU in
U us (0258)"). boot-arg sweetgputlbi=1: an invalidate after every page, as before.

